DoliSciGuaranteeActStandardText = <b>JOINT AND SEVERAL GUARANTEE ACT (ACTE DE CAUTIONNEMENT SOLIDAIRE)</b><br><br>The undersigned, acting as guarantor and signatory of this deed, expressly declares to stand as personal and joint guarantor for the tenant designated in the contract (principal debtor), waiving the benefits of discussion and division, for all obligations arising from the lease granted by the landlord designated at the head hereof.<br><br>This undertaking guarantees the payment of rent, recoverable charges, occupancy indemnities, tenant repairs and any legal costs for the dwelling referred to in this contract, as from the stated effective date.<br><br>The guaranteed monthly rent amount corresponds to the principal amount stipulated in the contract, revisable annually according to the Rent Reference Index (IRL) published by INSEE.<br><br>Pursuant to Article 22-1 of the Law of July 6, 1989:<br>"Where the guarantee of obligations resulting from a lease contract concluded pursuant to this title does not specify any duration or where the duration of the guarantee is stipulated to be indefinite, the guarantor may terminate it unilaterally. Termination takes effect at the end of the lease contract, whether it is the initial contract or a renewed or extended contract, during which the landlord receives notification of the termination."
